<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre de Castelnau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1208</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Peter of Castelnau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre de Castelnau was a Cistercian monk and papal legate sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a> to combat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Catharism</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a>. After excommunicating Raymond VI of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, he was murdered near Saint-Gilles in January 1208 by a man thought to be one of the count's retainers. Innocent blamed Raymond and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-de-castelnau.jpg" alt="Pierre de Castelnau" width="246" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, French · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castelnou-assassinat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
